ntary beyond the rule itself.\n\n", "type": "thinking"}, {"text": "- **Reference-Frame Precedence for Superordinate Disease Nouns**\n  - **IF** a disease mention is a bare, unqualified, category-level noun (a broad family label, not a named entity) **and** its clause anchors it to a particular individual or case instance, meaning the grammatical subject is a patient or case participant and the noun names a condition that participant presents with, develops, or is diagnosed with (for example, through a presentation or diagnosis predicate or a \"with/as\" complement),\n  - **THEN** label it **SpecificDisease**, regardless of the lexical generality of the head noun.\n  - **Counter-case:** If the same kind of noun appears in a non-episodic, type-level description, such as a generic statement about a class of conditions or the defining features of a syndrome with no individual participant, label it **DiseaseClass**.\n  - **Negative Constraint (does NOT apply when):**\n    - the mention is a named entity (eponym, acronym, or named syndrome), which defaults to SpecificDisease independent of reference frame;\n    - the disease term functions as an attributive or prepositional modifier of another noun phrase, in which case the Modifier definition governs;\n    - the mention is part of a composite span, in which case the CompositeMention definition governs span-level labeling and this rule applies only to the individual head where that is defined;\n    - the noun carries an explicit category-denoting qualifier (e.g., a \"type of,\" \"class of,\" or \"group of\" construction), which keeps the label **DiseaseClass** even inside an episodic sentence.", "type": "text"}], "diagnostics": null, "model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "role": "assistant", "stop_details": null, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "type": "message", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens